<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Shah Nawaz Bhutto</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1888">1888</a>–<a href="/years/1957">1957</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Sir Shah Nawaz Bhutto</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Shah Nawaz Bhutto was a politician from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sindh">Sindh</a> who became <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/diwan">diwan</a>, or chief minister, of Junagadh State in 1947. He advised the Nawab <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mahabat-khanji-iii">Mahabat Khanji III</a> to accede to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pakistan">Pakistan</a>, a decision overturned when <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a> took control of the state later that year. He was the father of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zulfikar-ali-bhutto">Zulfikar Ali Bhutto</a>, later Prime Minister of Pakistan.</p></div>
